        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "47a6c217-6abb-5643-8f34-7c7677596754",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Ironweed\n- People: Lauro Escorel, Hector Babenco\n- Places: Albany, New York, Jay Street at Lark Street, Albany Rural Cemetery, Miss Albany Diner, North Broadway, 893 Broadway\n- Buildings: Miss Albany Diner, Lil's Diner\n\nFacts:\n- Miss Albany Diner, formerly known as Lil's Diner, is a historic diner in Albany, New York, built in 1941 and located at 893 Broadway on one of Albany's oldest streets.\n- Ironweed was released in 1987.\n- Ironweed is a film by Hector Babenco.\n- Ironweed made Lauro Escorel more widely known internationally.\n- Major portions of Ironweed were shot on location in Albany, New York, including Jay Street at Lark Street, Albany Rural Cemetery, and the Miss Albany Diner on North Broadway.",
